This directory contains a demo application that uses a stripped-down version of 
GFunctionIndividual to illustrate various advanced aspects of optimization with 
the Geneva library collection. It also shows how an individual registers options of its own
in its configuration file (GFMinIndividual::describeConfig(), through common's GParserBuilder).

The example has no main() of its own: it is a runtime-loadable module, libGFMinIndividual.so,
that the generic optimizer of example 18 loads:

  GGenericOptimizer --individual ./libGFMinIndividual.so

GFMinIndividual.{hpp,cpp} hold the individual; GFMinIndividualPlugin.cpp is only the module's
entry point (gem_module_manifest(), which names the individual's factory and its configuration
file).

